    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0584" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1731/66a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-10T20:00:00-04:00">September 10, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Public notice of intention to negotiate a foreign trade agreement with
                    Nicaragua was given September 7.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d503-f1"/> Please inform
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d503-f1" n="32" xml:id="d503-f1-content">
                <p>For text of public notice and statistics on trade with Nicaragua, issued by the
                    Department of State, September 7, 1934, see Department of State, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, September 8, 1934, pp. 170–179.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
